# Architecture overview

> Optional, human-owned project map. Explain responsibility and permitted
> dependencies; generated reference facts do not define architecture authority.

## Modules and responsibility

| Module | Responsibility | Owning boundary | Why this boundary exists |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |

## Allowed dependency directions

Describe the permitted directions between project-level modules and the reason
for each constraint. Record deliberate exceptions and their owner. Do not
require a full class-level graph.

## Complex subsystems

Link a separate `architecture/<subsystem>.md` only when a subsystem needs more
detail than this overview. Keep the overview at project level.

## Important decisions

Link relevant `architecture/adr-NNNN-<slug>.md` records when they exist. Keep
tradeoffs and decision status in each ADR; this map describes the current
structure. Omit this section when no ADR is needed.

## Extracted facts

Optional generated facts live separately under `reports/architecture-facts/`.
Label extractor, source snapshot, scope and limitations. Explicit resource,
path or type references are evidence of references, not proof of allowed
dependencies, runtime ownership or architectural intent.

## Maintenance

Update this map when a change alters module responsibility or an allowed
dependency direction. Ordinary implementation changes do not require a new
diagram. Resolve conflicts with Product, Coding Rules and approved decisions;
do not silently replace human intent with generated output.
